          "Human PBMCs were pre-isolated from EDTA anticoagulated peripheral blood via Ficoll density gradient centrifugation and cryopreserved long-term. Cryopreserved PBMCs were quickly thawed at 37 \u00b0C, washed with warm RPMI medium to remove DMSO, then purified with cold PBS + 0.04% BSA, and qualified with >90% cell viability.",
          "Library was performed according to the manufacter\u2019s instructions (single cell 5\u2019 v3 protocol, 10x Genomics).Cell suspension was adjusted to 700\u20131200 cells/\u03bcL and loaded onto 10x Genomics Chromium Next GEM Chip G to generate single-cell GEM droplets. Within each GEM, cell lysis, polyA mRNA capture via 16 bp barcode + 12 bp UMI poly(dT) gel bead oligos, and in-droplet reverse transcription were completed for single-cell RNA extraction, following Lianchuan Biotechnology\u2019s 10x scRNA-seq experimental protocol."
